# Third-party material

This licence (MIT, see [LICENSE](LICENSE)) covers this project's own code. Two things that ship in
this repository are somebody else's:

## `vendor/openpgp-5.11.3.min.js` — OpenPGP.js

* Upstream: <https://github.com/openpgpjs/openpgpjs>
* Version: 5.11.3, file `dist/openpgp.min.js` (the browser UMD build)
* Licence: **LGPL-3.0-or-later**. The licence text is kept in
  [`vendor/LICENSE.LGPL-3.0.txt`](vendor/LICENSE.LGPL-3.0.txt).
* The built command `share-selected-text.js` **embeds** this library, so the bundle as shipped is
  LGPL-3.0-or-later code carrying MIT code, not MIT alone. Its sha256 is pinned in `build.mjs`, and
  `vendor/README.md` documents why this build (and not the Node one) is vendored.

